WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.600
Plotly.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.878
Some charts are meant to be read.

3
00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:05.795
Others are meant to be explored.

4
00:00:05.795 --> 00:00:07.233
Plotly is for exploring.

5
00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:12.633
Plotly renders charts as interactive HTML and JavaScript.

6
00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:19.567
Hover for per-point detail, zoom and pan into dense regions, and click legend entries to toggle series.

7
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:27.133
Plotly express gives one-liner figures from a DataFrame, and graph objects is the control layer for when you outgrow it.

8
00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:29.800
Here's the interactivity.

9
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.267
Hover over any point to see its details.

10
00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.867
Zoom and pan into crowded regions.

11
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:38.133
And click the legend to toggle whole series on or off.

12
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:40.533
So which should you use?

13
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:42.400
It depends on the audience.

14
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.482
A human exploring results wants Plotly.

15
00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:50.333
A paper, a README, or a CI artifact wants a static matplotlib image.

16
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:52.233
Pick the tool for the audience.

17
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:54.600
Here's one in code.

18
00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:01.867
Plotly express takes a DataFrame, picks the columns for each axis, colors by a flag, and uses a log scale.

19
00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:06.300
The hover name and hover data decide what appears when you point at a dot.

20
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.733
Then write html produces one file anyone can open, no Python required.

21
00:01:12.933 --> 00:01:13.900
A real case.

22
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.600
In the weekly Mission Control review, the team opens your asteroid scatter.

23
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:24.667
They hover for names, and zoom into the corner closer than the moon, where the interesting objects hide.

24
00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:27.700
Nobody asks you to re-run it with labels.

25
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.167
The same chart is embedded in the FastAPI dashboard.

26
00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.185
Let's recap.

27
00:01:33.185 --> 00:01:35.367
Plotly makes interactive charts.

28
00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:39.100
Express gives one-liners, graph objects gives control.

29
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.800
Write html makes a shareable file.

30
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.164
And pick the tool by audience.

31
00:01:44.164 --> 00:01:45.333
Next up: Seaborn.
